{"case_id":"T8062","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics","attack_surface"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["security_compute_user_raw"],"reason":"H0 only fuzzes the CIL compilation-to-policydb pipeline and never calls the changed libselinux entry point security_compute_user_raw. It therefore cannot exercise parsing of the user-interface reply read from selinux_mnt/user, including attacker- or fault-shaped nel values, NUL-separated context entries, truncated replies, and allocation-size behavior addressed by the new calloc and ptr bounds check.","evidence":["H0 invokes cil_add_file, cil_compile, cil_build_policydb, sepol_policydb_optimize, and sepol_policydb_write; it does not invoke security_compute_user_raw or any libselinux user-query API.","security_compute_user_raw constructs \"%s/user\" from selinux_mnt and exchanges data through open, write, and read, creating filesystem/API state absent from H0.","The reply parser obtains nel with sscanf(buf, \"%u\", &nel), allocates ary with calloc((size_t)nel + 1, sizeof(char *)), and walks NUL-terminated entries using strdup(ptr) and ptr += strlen(ptr) + 1.","The source change explicitly handles a bogus very large nel and a claimed entry count exceeding the reply contents, demonstrating fuzz-relevant count, allocation, truncation, and delimiter semantics not represented by H0's single CIL source byte stream."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated harness for security_compute_user_raw with controlled selinux_mnt/user I/O (for example, mocked or interposed open/write/read). Fuzz scon and user plus raw reply bytes, emphasizing extreme nel values, missing or extra NUL separators, truncated context lists, empty entries, maximum-page replies, and read/write failures; assert clean success or failure and safely free any returned con array."}
